 "command": "bash research_loop/results/DIAG-PERDOC/launch_perdoc.sh ; then bash research_loop/results/DIAG-PERDOC/launch_perdoc_phase3.sh ; then research_loop/results/DIAG-PERDOC/finalize.py. Data prep (CPU, no GPU): research_loop/results/DIAG-PERDOC/prep_perdoc.py -> /tmp/perdoc/{synth,eval}. 11 single-document AM Phase-2 writes at the canonical top-32 point (5 documents x 2 rotary bases + 1 reference-draw replicate), SYNTH_DATA_PATH pointed at a parquet filtered to ONE paper title, and 70 standalone eval_forgetting.py evals. NO source file edited (MECH-KEYS was editing cartridges/am/key_select.py, which differed from HEAD throughout). Imports AND driver pinned to /tmp/amsnap_perdoc (git archive HEAD {cartridges,examples} at 5bbcbf0a; manifest sha256 8bf3b174..., re-verified unchanged after both phases while repo HEAD moved 5bbcbf0a -> d1dbf7cd mid-run); cartridges.__file__ = /tmp/amsnap_perdoc/cartridges printed from cwd=/tmp in both wrapper logs. GPU 0 claimed via flock.",
 "observations": "THE ANSWER IS THE OPPOSITE OF BOTH BRANCHES THE BRIEF ANTICIPATED: a document written ALONE into 32 uncontested slots is not better than, and not equal to, the same document written as one of 16 - it is MUCH WORSE on its own eval questions. Pooled over the five documents (27 questions, 1164 scored tokens), the solo caches give 3.7488 against the 16-document cartridge's 2.6186 and the Phase-1 floor's 3.9640; the paired per-document gap is +1.101 (sd 0.186, se 0.083) and it has the same sign in 5/5 documents, range +0.882 to +1.303. The 15 OTHER documents are therefore not competing the target document out of the cartridge - they are supplying most of what the model uses to answer it. Writing a document alone buys only -0.201 (se 0.064) on its own questions, 15.5% of the -1.302 (se 0.143) that the full 16-document write buys on those same questions; k=12 buys -1.421, more than k=16, on the same subsets. THE SECOND ARM AGREES: at the corrected rotary base (AM_ROPE_THETA=5000000, the config the brief named) the solo write is much stronger, -0.665 (se 0.092) on own questions, but still +0.753 (sd 0.076, se 0.034) WORSE than that arm's own 16-document cartridge, again 5/5 documents. UNCERTAINTY, MEASURED NOT ASSUMED: these subsets are 3-7 questions / 52-312 scored tokens, so the +/-0.15 full-set band does not apply. Two nominally identical solo writes of doc-015, differing only in which 32 of its 532 synthesis conversations were drawn as reference queries (3/32 overlap; the two caches differ in 36/180 tensors, 27.8% relative Frobenius in layer 0's values), gave 3.8955 vs 4.1118 on that subset - a same-condition spread of 0.216 - and 3.6313 vs 3.5837 on the full MT set (0.048). A leave-one-out decomposition recovering doc-015's seven per-example losses exactly gives a per-example sd of 1.58 but a PAIRED solo-minus-16-document delta of +1.172 (sd 0.597, se 0.226) with 0/7 questions favouring the solo write. So the headline gap is 5x to 14x the noise it must clear, while the per-document ordering (doc-011 +1.284 vs doc-000 +0.882) is NOT resolvable at this sample size. PROVENANCE IS EXACT, NOT ASSERTED: writing doc-1 alone through the filtered-parquet route produced a cache BITWISE IDENTICAL to the canonical run's cache-after-doc-000 across all 180 tensors and reproduced DIAG-SEQUENCE's k=1 full-MT loss 3.7445480823516846 to all 16 digits; the same holds for the theta=5e6 arm against DIAG-ROPE arm B's own doc-000 snapshot. The three reference checkpoints re-measured in this session reproduce the board exactly (Phase-1 3.7825491428375244, k=12 2.435236930847168, k=16 2.5524158477783203, k=16 theta=5e6 2.529625177383423). The canonical document prompt built from the filtered parquet is byte-identical (sha256) to the in-sequence one for all five documents, so only the reference DRAW differs for documents other than the first. Subset arithmetic is exact by construction - per-example CE is packing-invariant (block-diagonal seq_ids, packing never splits an element) and the harness loss is a token-weighted mean - and the empirical check agrees to 0.0061 (union of the five subsets: 3.9701 measured vs 3.9640 predicted). BANDWIDTH IS NOT THE DIFFERENCE: every solo write lands mean ref mass_on_S of 0.1477-0.1535 on its written slots, indistinguishable from the 16-document run's 0.15851, and its own solve MSE is 0.0085-0.2046 (theta=1e4) / 0.0141-0.0192 (theta=5e6). A solo write is a well-fitted, equally-well-routed write that simply does not carry the content. MOST OF WHAT A SOLO WRITE DOES BUY IS OFF-TARGET: decomposing each solo cache's full-MT loss into its own questions and the other 15 documents' questions, 71%-93% of the full-MT improvement lands on documents that were never written (doc-000: own -0.050 vs others -0.037, 93% off-target; doc-015: own -0.394 vs others -0.121, 71%). ONE FINDING OUTSIDE THE ASSIGNED QUESTION, RECORDED BECAUSE THE GATES FORCED IT INTO VIEW: the rotary base is NOT a wash at small k. One document alone takes full MT from 3.7825 to 3.1146 at theta=5e6 versus 3.7445 at theta=1e4 - a first-document gain of 0.668 vs 0.038, 17.6x - yet the two arms converge to 2.5296 vs 2.5524 at k=16 and 2.4705 vs 2.4352 at k=12. Both k=1 numbers come from stock snapshots of runs already on the board and reproduce bitwise here, so this is not a new run and not an artefact of this task's route; DIAG-ROPE's '\u0394MT -0.019, inside noise' was measured only at k=16. CAVEATS: five of sixteen documents (chosen as the brief specified: the earliest, the latest, and the two largest subsets, plus one more 5-question document), one seed, no QA axis, and the solo writes for documents other than the first use a different draw of 32 reference conversations than their in-sequence counterparts (1-4 of 32 overlap) - the doc-015 replicate bounds that at 0.216 on a per-document subset."
